%N A094778 "Dropping time" in juggler sequence problem starting at 2n+1 (number of steps to reach a lower number than starting value).
%C A094778 From _Philippe Cochin_, Sep 28 2026: (Start)
%C A094778 For n >= 1, let o(k) be the number of odd terms among the first k terms of the juggler trajectory of 2n+1 (A094683), and let t be the least k with 3^o(k) < 2^k. Then a(n) <= t, and t = A020914(o(t)). - _Philippe Cochin_, Sep 28 2026
%C A094778 a(n) = t for all n < 5*10^5. It is not known whether a(n) < t can occur.
%C A094778 (End)
%H A094778 Philippe Cochin, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22864933">Five-Step Descent Certificates for the Juggler Map: Parity Statistics of Nested Floor Powers</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%e A094778 9 -> 27 -> 140 -> 11 -> 36 -> 6, taking 5 steps, so a(4) = 5.
%Y A094778 Cf. A007320, A020914, A094683.
%Y A094778 Collatz analogs: A126241, A260590.
%K A094778 easy,nonn
